  "notes": "Pop-punk with hip-hop swagger and synth colour: 135–178 straight, backbeat on 2&4 at speed, with the later singles slowing to 135–150. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"8th kick, snare 2&4, hat 8ths\" with \"handclaps layered on the backbeat in the chorus\" (the clap offset tightened plus a snap lane), \"a 16th snare-roll lift into **every** chorus\" — which is why `fills.smallEveryBars` is 4 with the ladder on and the hat rolls run at 0.4, the busiest lift schedule in this batch — and \"occasional drum-machine intro before the band enters\", which is why the humanize keeps a tight grid for a live kit. The bass is \"root 8ths\" with \"a slap/octave figure on the funk-leaning verses\", so the octave and fifth are its passing tones. Harmony is D-flat/C/B majors over I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V \"with a minor-key verse into a major chorus on the darker singles\", which is why the minor cycle is authored alongside them and both modes carry weight in the scales. The topline is \"nasal, syllable-dense in the verse (near-rapped) and anthemic in the chorus\", i.e. the 4–11 density. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it medium-high and says the drum detail is partly convention-based. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 150.",
